WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.796
That first morning at school, Sara noticed a plump, blond girl about the same age as Sara.

2
00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:11.870
The girl was chewing on the ribbon of her pigtail and staring at Sara.

3
00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:17.076
When Monsieur Dufarge spoke to Sara, the plump girl looked a little frightened.

4
00:00:17.077 --> 00:00:22.816
When Sara replied in French, the girl gave a startled jump and turned red.

5
00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:27.556
Miss Minchin was still in a bad mood about Sara's perfect French.

6
00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:31.200
"Miss St. John, stop chewing on your ribbon!

7
00:00:31.201 --> 00:00:34.338
And sit up at once!" she snapped.

8
00:00:34.339 --> 00:00:37.002
The girl gave another startled jump.

9
00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:43.818
Lavinia and Jessie giggled, and the girl turned redder than ever.

10
00:00:43.819 --> 00:00:47.665
Sara's father often remarked on Sara's soft heart.

11
00:00:47.666 --> 00:00:53.398
"Sara always wants to fight when she sees people in trouble," he liked to say.

12
00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.087
And that was certainly true now.

13
00:00:58.088 --> 00:01:04.067
"Those girls shouldn't laugh," thought Sara. "That's mean."

14
00:01:04.068 --> 00:01:10.400
But Lavinia and Jessie continued to snicker when the girl spoke in French for Monsieur Dufarge.

15
00:01:10.401 --> 00:01:16.143
Sara felt sorry for this girl, who had such trouble saying the French words correctly.

16
00:01:16.144 --> 00:01:20.621
The French lessons were obviously quite difficult for her.

17
00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:28.284
When the morning's lessons were finally finished, the plump girl sat on a window seat, looking miserable.

18
00:01:28.285 --> 00:01:30.695
Sara went over to her.

19
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:33.622
"What's your name?" asked Sara.

20
00:01:33.623 --> 00:01:37.185
The girl seemed amazed that Sara was talking to her.

21
00:01:37.186 --> 00:01:43.367
"My name is Ermengarde St. John," she replied.

22
00:01:43.368 --> 00:01:49.161
"Mine is Sara Crewe. What a pretty name you have!" exclaimed Sara.

23
00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:52.522
"It sounds like a name from a story."

24
00:01:52.523 --> 00:01:54.427
"I like your name too.

25
00:01:54.428 --> 00:01:58.841
Where did you learn to speak French?" Ermengarde asked.

26
00:01:58.842 --> 00:02:02.757
"Oh, I've done it all my life," Sara answered.

27
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:07.129
"If you'd always heard French at home, you could do it too."

28
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:13.896
"No, I don't think so," said Ermengarde sadly. "I'm not very smart."

29
00:02:13.897 --> 00:02:18.824
Ermengarde explained that her father spoke seven or eight languages.

30
00:02:18.825 --> 00:02:26.370
He had a huge library filled with thousands of books and couldn't understand why Ermengarde didn't do well in school.

31
00:02:26.371 --> 00:02:30.573
He had told Miss Minchin that Ermengarde must be made to learn.

32
00:02:30.574 --> 00:02:36.262
But at school Ermengarde was often in trouble or in tears.

33
00:02:36.263 --> 00:02:40.643
"You're smart, aren't you?" Ermengarde said to Sara.

34
00:02:40.644 --> 00:02:44.399
Sara looked out the window into the dirty square.

35
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.338
She could see some sparrows hopping along iron railings.

36
00:02:48.339 --> 00:02:53.208
She thought for a minute. "Oh, I don't know."

37
00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:58.370
Then suddenly she changed the subject. "Would you like to meet Emily?"

38
00:02:58.371 --> 00:03:01.417
"Who's Emily?" asked Ermengarde.

39
00:03:01.418 --> 00:03:06.340
"Come up to my room and see," replied Sara.

40
00:03:06.341 --> 00:03:09.690
Ermengarde followed Sara upstairs.

41
00:03:09.691 --> 00:03:15.779
"Is it true," she asked, "that you have a playroom all to yourself?"

42
00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:21.111
"Yes," Sara answered. "Papa asked Miss Minchin to let me have one.

43
00:03:21.112 --> 00:03:23.723
It's because I like to tell myself stories.

44
00:03:23.724 --> 00:03:28.152
And the mood gets spoiled if I know people are listening."

45
00:03:28.153 --> 00:03:31.737
Sara stopped outside the door to her room.

46
00:03:31.738 --> 00:03:37.344
"If we're quiet, maybe we'll catch her," she said mysteriously.

47
00:03:37.345 --> 00:03:42.385
Ermengarde blinked. She had no idea what Sara was talking about.

48
00:03:42.386 --> 00:03:45.378
But Sara's eyes were full of fun.

49
00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:48.478
Ermengarde couldn't wait to see what happened.

50
00:03:48.479 --> 00:03:52.752
Sara threw open the door.

51
00:03:52.753 --> 00:03:57.708
Ermengarde saw a beautiful doll sitting on a chair in front of the fire.

52
00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:03.221
"Oh, Emily is back in her seat!" Sara sounded disappointed.

53
00:04:03.222 --> 00:04:07.287
"Can she walk?" asked Ermengarde in surprise.

54
00:04:07.288 --> 00:04:13.638
"I like to pretend she can," said Sara. "Don't you pretend such things?"

55
00:04:13.639 --> 00:04:22.216
"No." Ermengarde was in awe of this strange girl. "Never. May I hold Emily?"

56
00:04:22.217 --> 00:04:27.629
"Of course," said Sara. "And I'll tell you stories."

57
00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.563
So they sat together.

58
00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:35.641
Her green eyes shining, Sara told Ermengarde all about the secret life of dolls.

59
00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:40.437
She also talked about life in India and the voyage to England.

60
00:04:40.438 --> 00:04:46.248
When Sara got to the part about finding Emily in the toy shop, she suddenly looked upset.

61
00:04:46.249 --> 00:04:50.806
Ermengarde had the feeling that Sara was bravely trying not to cry.

62
00:04:50.807 --> 00:04:54.888
"What's wrong?" she asked in alarm.

63
00:04:54.889 --> 00:04:59.896
"Do you love your father more than anything in the world?" Sara burst out.

64
00:04:59.897 --> 00:05:03.350
Ermengarde thought this was a strange question.

65
00:05:03.351 --> 00:05:08.937
"I hardly ever see him. He's always in his library reading things."

66
00:05:08.938 --> 00:05:16.716
"Oh, I love my father and miss him so." Sara buried her head in her hands.

67
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:19.674
Ermengarde's mouth fell open a little.

68
00:05:19.675 --> 00:05:24.070
Sara was so wonderful and different from anyone else.

69
00:05:24.071 --> 00:05:26.282
Sara lifted her head.

70
00:05:26.283 --> 00:05:31.190
"If I keep telling you stories, I won't miss him as much."

71
00:05:31.191 --> 00:05:37.177
Tears came to Ermengarde's eyes, and she felt a lump in her throat.

72
00:05:37.178 --> 00:05:39.977
"Lavinia and Jessie are best friends.

73
00:05:39.978 --> 00:05:42.514
Do you think we could be best friends?

74
00:05:42.515 --> 00:05:48.444
You're so smart, and I'm not smart at all. But I like you very much!"

75
00:05:48.445 --> 00:05:54.516
"Of course we can be best friends," said Sara. Her face lit up.

76
00:05:54.517 --> 00:06:03.728
"And do you know what, Ermengarde? I can help you with your French lessons!"

